5.2 Evidence vocabulary

• OBSERVED: traceable report, measurement, or witnessed performance; report limitations.
• GIVEN: premise explicitly supplied for the example, not independently verified.
• INFERRED: explanation supported by evidence but not uniquely entailed.
• HYPOTHESIS: testable conjecture with uncertain support.
• TRANSFER: mapping into another domain awaiting its own validation.
• SYMBOLIC: analogy or metaphor; not an empirical claim.
• TESTED: a named test was actually conducted and its result recorded.
• UNKNOWN: insufficient evidence; do not fill by invention.
• CONTRADICTED: evidence opposes the claim; preserve reason and scope.

Never silently upgrade GIVEN, INFERRED, SYMBOLIC, or TRANSFER to TESTED.

